WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.020
"Many years ago, the great British explorer George Mallory,

00:00:04.160 --> 00:00:07.560
who was to die on Mount Everest,

00:00:07.660 --> 00:00:10.160
was asked, "why did he want to climb it?"

00:00:10.200 --> 00:00:12.300
He said "because it is there".

00:00:12.580 --> 00:00:15.300
Well space is there, and we're going to climb it.

00:00:15.640 --> 00:00:18.220
And the moon and the planets are there,

00:00:18.240 --> 00:00:20.700
and new hopes for knowledge and peace are there.

00:00:21.320 --> 00:00:28.880
And therefore, as we set sail, we ask God's blessing on the most hazardous and dangerous and

00:00:28.900 --> 00:00:31.460
greatest adventure on which man has ever embarked."

00:00:31.460 --> 00:00:32.480
- President John F. Kennedy

00:01:03.520 --> 00:01:05.480
"Look at the stars,

00:01:05.480 --> 00:01:09.800
the great kings of the past look down on us from those stars."

00:01:10.420 --> 00:01:11.300
"Really?"

00:01:11.640 --> 00:01:12.140
"Yes."

00:01:12.740 --> 00:01:14.700
"So whenever you feel alone

00:01:14.980 --> 00:01:16.400
just remember,

00:01:16.620 --> 00:01:19.640
those kings will always be there to guide you."

00:01:19.900 --> 00:01:22.000
- The Lion King (1994)

00:01:31.600 --> 00:01:34.860
"There is a tingling in the spine, a catch in the voice,

00:01:35.560 --> 00:01:39.040
a faint sensation, as if a distant memory,

00:01:39.040 --> 00:01:41.260
of falling, from a great height.

00:01:41.880 --> 00:01:45.120
We know you're approaching the grandest of mysteries."

00:01:45.260 --> 00:01:46.340
- Carl Sagan (Cosmos, 1980)

00:01:58.780 --> 00:02:00.640
"Old books?"

00:02:01.180 --> 00:02:03.320
"Stories written before space travel,

00:02:03.320 --> 00:02:04.000
but,

00:02:04.000 --> 00:02:05.940
about, space travel."

00:02:06.800 --> 00:02:10.560
"How could there have been stories about space travel, before - - ?"

00:02:11.060 --> 00:02:13.000
"The writers," Pris said.

00:02:13.420 --> 00:02:14.860
"They made it up."

00:02:14.860 --> 00:02:15.940
- Philip K. Dick (Do Androids Dream of Electric Sheep? 1968)

00:02:41.180 --> 00:02:42.880
"What is it you want, Mary?"

00:02:43.040 --> 00:02:45.400
"What do you want, y-you want the moon?"

00:02:45.900 --> 00:02:48.840
"Just say the word and I'll throw a lasso around it and pull it down."

00:02:49.460 --> 00:02:51.120
"Hey that's a pretty good idea."

00:02:51.680 --> 00:02:52.720
"I'll give you the moon, Mary."

00:02:52.980 --> 00:02:53.700
"I'll take it."

00:02:53.800 --> 00:02:54.680
- It's a Wonderful Life (1946)

00:02:55.560 --> 00:02:58.020
That's one small step for man,

